  "helpQ1": "What is iBeacon and what does the app use it for?",
  "helpA1": "Each exhibition area has an iBeacon device that sends a short-range Bluetooth signal. When you get close, the app picks up the signal, works out which artifact you're next to, and opens its introduction. You don't need to scan a code or type in an artifact number.",
  "helpQ2": "Where do I turn on scanning?",
  "helpA2": "Open the sidebar with the menu button in the top-left corner of the Explore page, then turn on the \"iBeacon scanning\" switch. The switch applies to the whole app and you can turn it off at any time.",
  "helpQ3": "Why isn't the app detecting any artifacts?",
  "helpA3": "Check in this order: is the \"iBeacon scanning\" switch in the sidebar on, is your phone's Bluetooth on, and has the app been given Bluetooth permission in your system settings? iBeacon signals only reach a few meters, so you also need to stand near the exhibit.",
  "helpQ4": "Does iBeacon scanning use a lot of battery?",
  "helpA4": "iBeacon uses Bluetooth Low Energy, which uses very little battery compared to GPS or 4G. Still, once you've finished your visit, turn the switch off in the sidebar to save even more.",
  "helpQ5": "Does the audio guide play automatically?",
  "helpA5": "Yes. When iBeacon detects that you're near an artifact, the app opens and plays that artifact's audio guide — you don't need to tap anything. To listen again or hear another artifact, open the artifact's page and tap \"Listen to the audio guide\" at the bottom of the About tab.",
  "helpQ6": "How do I mute it somewhere I need to be quiet?",
  "helpA6": "Tap the speaker button. It's in three places: the mini player at the bottom of the screen, the pop-up shown when a beacon detects an artifact, and the audio guide page. Muting only silences the sound — the guide keeps running and you can still read the text.",
  "helpQ7": "Can I change the playback speed?",
  "helpA7": "Yes. On the audio guide page, tap the speed button on the right of the controls to cycle through 0.75×, 1×, 1.25× and 1.5×.",
  "helpQ8": "Where do I change the audio guide language?",
  "helpA8": "Two ways: the translate button on the audio guide page, or My account → Language. The sidebar also has a Language item.",
  "helpQ9": "Can I still read the content after walking away from the artifact?",
  "helpA9": "Yes. Loaded content stays available even after you leave the beacon's range, so you can read it again after leaving the exhibition area.",
  "helpQ10": "Do I have to log in to use the app?",
  "helpA10": "No. Visitors can see all artifacts, the map, audio guides and notifications without an account.",
  "helpQ11": "So what is logging in for?",
  "helpA11": "To save your favorite artifacts and sync your data across devices. Your visit history is still saved on your phone even if you haven't logged in.",
  "helpQ12": "Where do I log in or sign up?",
  "helpA12": "Go to My account and use the \"Log in\" and \"Sign up\" buttons at the top of the page. The sidebar has the same shortcuts.",
  "helpQ13": "The map is blank — I can't see anything?",
  "helpA13": "The map needs an internet connection to load its background. Check your Wi-Fi or mobile data. Artifact pins still show in the right places even before the map background has loaded.",
  "helpQ14": "Why does the app ask for my location?",
  "helpA14": "Only to show your position on the heritage site map, so you know where you are relative to the artifacts. If you decline, the map and artifact pins still work normally.",
  "helpQ15": "Can I filter artifacts by exhibition area?",
  "helpA15": "Yes. On the Map tab there is a row of area buttons at the top; pick an area and the map only shows that area's pins.",
  "helpQ16": "Where can I see notifications I've received?",
  "helpA16": "Tap the bell in the top-right corner of the Explore page. The red number on the bell is how many notifications you haven't read.",
  "helpQ17": "I want to rate an artifact or give feedback about the site.",
  "helpA17": "For an artifact: open its page and go to the \"Reviews\" tab. For general feedback about the site: go to My account → Rate this heritage site.",
